# 02. Frontend Architecture

## 02.1 Architectural layers

The frontend follows this conceptual layering:

```text
Presentation Layer
        ↓
Page / Route Layer
        ↓
Feature Layer
        ↓
Domain UI Layer
        ↓
Shared Component Layer
        ↓
Data / API Layer
        ↓
State Management
        ↓
Backend
```

### Presentation Layer

Responsible for:

- visual rendering;
- responsive layout;
- typography;
- spacing;
- animation;
- accessibility presentation.

### Page / Route Layer

Responsible for:

- route entry;
- route-level loading;
- route-level error boundaries;
- resource identity;
- layout composition;
- authorization-aware rendering.

### Feature Layer

Responsible for:

- user-facing feature workflows;
- forms;
- mutations;
- filtering;
- local interaction logic;
- feature-specific state.

### Domain UI Layer

Responsible for reusable GrowFlow domain representations such as:

- project lifecycle;
- task;
- milestone;
- risk;
- health;
- activity;
- AI execution;
- document;
- assessment.

### Shared Component Layer

Responsible for generic UI primitives and common interaction patterns.

### Data / API Layer

Responsible for:

- API client;
- request serialization;
- response parsing;
- error normalization;
- cache/query behavior;
- mutation integration;
- authentication headers;
- SSE client.

### State Management

Separates:

```text
SERVER STATE
UI STATE
STREAMING STATE
```

---

# 03. State Architecture

## 03.1 Server State

Canonical examples:

- current user;
- role authorization;
- project;
- project definition;
- project instance;
- tasks;
- milestones;
- risks;
- documents;
- GitHub connection status;
- mentor notes;
- help requests;
- assessment results;
- blueprint;
- notifications;
- activity;
- analytics;
- AI execution records.

Server state should be fetched and reconciled through the API layer.

---

## 03.2 UI State

Examples:

- open modal;
- selected tab;
- expanded table row;
- filter values;
- sort direction;
- sidebar collapsed state;
- mobile drawer open/closed;
- temporary form values;
- selected items;
- local search text;
- confirmation dialog visibility.

UI state is not canonical domain state.

---

## 03.3 Streaming State

Examples:

- AI generation currently running;
- execution stage;
- progress events;
- SSE connection state;
- live notification arrival;
- document processing state;
- RAG processing state;
- background job status;
- reconnecting state.

Streaming state must reconcile back into server state.

---

## 03.4 State ownership rule

A piece of data must have one clear owner.

```text
Canonical business truth → Backend
Presentation representation → Frontend
Temporary interaction state → Frontend
Live event transport → Frontend streaming layer
```

The frontend must not create a second canonical version of business truth.

