# 06. Design-System Implementation

## 06.1 Visual identity

The frozen visual direction is:

> Soft Intelligence

Core characteristics:

- calm;
- restrained;
- warm;
- precise;
- editorial;
- operational;
- information-dense without visual noise.

---

## 06.2 Appearance

Default:

```text
Soft white / warm light
```

Dark counterpart:

```text
Soft charcoal
```

Dark mode is not a simple color inversion.

Both modes must preserve:

- hierarchy;
- contrast;
- surface relationships;
- semantic status meaning;
- visual identity.

---

## 06.3 Typography

Use a Manrope-style geometric humanist sans direction.

Typography hierarchy must distinguish:

- page title;
- section title;
- subsection;
- body;
- labels;
- metadata;
- helper text;
- numerical metrics;
- code;
- AI/system messages.

Do not make every piece of text large or bold.

---

## 06.4 Color

Use:

- muted neutrals;
- one subtle primary accent;
- restrained semantic colors;
- a slightly deeper AI variant.

Avoid:

- rainbow role themes;
- neon AI;
- excessive gradients;
- decorative color everywhere.

---

## 06.5 Surfaces

Surface hierarchy should be quiet.

Preferred:

- background separation;
- subtle borders;
- restrained shadows;
- spacing;
- typography;
- grouping.

Avoid card-everything design.

---

## 06.6 Cards

Cards are used when they establish meaningful grouping.

Cards should not exist merely because the component library has a Card component.

---

## 06.7 Tables

Tables are first-class operational interfaces.

They should support:

- dense rows;
- clear headers;
- sortable columns where meaningful;
- filters;
- pagination;
- status;
- row actions;
- responsive behavior;
- keyboard access.

Tables should feel integrated into the page rather than floating as unrelated boxes.

---

## 06.8 AI visual language

AI surfaces are slightly deeper visually than normal application surfaces.

AI styling may use:

- deeper tonal hierarchy;
- clear execution indicators;
- structured output blocks;
- controlled motion.

Avoid:

- glowing neon interfaces;
- fake typing effects;
- endless animated gradients;
- anthropomorphic decoration that hides system state.

---

# 07. Motion

## 07.1 Public experience

Public website motion can be more expressive.

Hero interaction follows:

```text
Float → Settle
```

Motion should feel physical and intentional.

---

## 07.2 Authenticated experience

Motion is subordinate to productivity.

Use:

- subtle entrance;
- small state transitions;
- restrained hover/focus;
- controlled progress animation;
- meaningful movement.

Do not animate every component.

---

## 07.3 Reduced motion

Respect reduced-motion preferences.

When reduced motion is enabled:

- remove nonessential movement;
- reduce parallax;
- reduce transition distance;
- preserve functional feedback without animation dependency.

