# 36. Performance

## 36.1 Initial load

Optimize:

- critical assets;
- JavaScript size;
- fonts;
- images;
- above-the-fold rendering.

## 36.2 Route loading

Use appropriate code splitting/lazy loading for large workplace areas.

Admin observability pages should not unnecessarily inflate public/student bundles.

## 36.3 Tables

For large datasets use appropriate:

- pagination;
- virtualization;
- server-side filtering;
- server-side sorting.

## 36.4 Images

Use:

- appropriate dimensions;
- modern formats where supported;
- lazy loading;
- meaningful alt text.

## 36.5 Charts

Charts must not become a major performance bottleneck.

## 36.6 SSE

Avoid unnecessary simultaneous connections.

Connection ownership should follow authenticated application/session needs rather than every component opening its own connection.

---

# 37. Error-Boundary Strategy

Recommended hierarchy:

```text
Application Boundary
    ↓
Role Boundary
    ↓
Feature Boundary
    ↓
Page Boundary
    ↓
Component Boundary
```

A failure in one feature should not unnecessarily crash the entire authenticated workplace.

---

# 38. Loading / Empty / Error / Success Rules

Every data-dependent surface must explicitly define:

### Loading

Use skeletons/placeholders that preserve layout where possible.

### Empty

Explain:

- what is empty;
- why it may be empty;
- what action can create/populate it.

### Error

Explain:

- what failed;
- whether retry is safe;
- what the user can do next.

### Success

Confirm meaningful mutations without excessive toast spam.

### Processing

For background operations, distinguish:

```text
Not started
Queued
Processing
Completed
Failed
```

Do not use an indefinite generic spinner for long-running workflows.

