# 48. Critical Acceptance Scenarios

The frontend is not considered complete if these fail:

1. User can enter the correct workplace.
2. Unauthorized workplace access is blocked.
3. Separate Login and Sign Up behave correctly.
4. Deep links survive authentication.
5. Student can reach project workspace.
6. Project lifecycle is represented consistently.
7. Assessment can complete.
8. Blueprint generation can show queued/running/completed/failed states.
9. Leaving the page does not kill background AI work.
10. Returning to a project reconciles current job state.
11. Mentor can distinguish Project Definitions from Project Instances.
12. Definition edits do not silently change instances.
13. Project changes show impact before mutation.
14. Notifications deep-link correctly.
15. Search respects authorization.
